('industrial-high-dusting','Industrial high dusting','A considered approach to complex overhead environments.','manufacturing','Industrial dust removal starts with understanding the facility. Tell us what your operation produces, where dust collects and what access restrictions apply so the cleaning method can be assessed before work is scheduled.', ['Production-area overhead structures and equipment exteriors','Dust identification and site-specific method assessment','Operating windows, planned shutdowns and exclusion zones']),
('warehouse-high-dusting','Warehouse high dusting','A cleaner facility. From the rafters down.','hero','Warehouse ceilings collect dust well beyond the reach of everyday janitorial work. Build a targeted scope for the structures above your aisles, inventory and loading areas, with access coordinated around the way your warehouse runs.', ['Distribution centres, storage facilities and logistics buildings','Beams, trusses, rafters and elevated horizontal surfaces','Lift access, floor loading and aisle clearance assessment']),
('ceiling-cleaning','Ceiling & overhead cleaning','Give the overlooked areas the attention they need.','overhead','From exposed roof structures to elevated fixtures, overhead cleaning focuses on surfaces that routine floor-level cleaning does not reach. The method is selected for the surface, dust and access conditions.', ['Ceiling structures and accessible overhead surfaces','Cobweb removal and targeted dry dust extraction','Protection of the equipment and activity below']),
('rafter-beam-cleaning','Rafter & beam cleaning','Take care of what collects above your operation.','overhead','Rafters, joists, beams and trusses offer long horizontal surfaces where dust can settle. A planned high-access clean addresses those surfaces while considering overhead obstructions and the areas underneath.', ['Steel beams, joists, rafters and roof trusses','Horizontal ledges and structural connections','Reach assessment and appropriate access equipment']),
('pipe-conduit-cleaning','Pipe & conduit cleaning','Detail work for intricate overhead services.','overhead','Pipes, conduits and cable trays call for a careful, surface-specific scope. We assess access and coordinate with your facility team around sensitive systems and any required isolation.', ['Accessible pipe and conduit exteriors','Cable tray exterior surfaces where suitable','Sprinkler-adjacent work subject to system protection requirements']),
('duct-exterior-cleaning','Duct exterior cleaning','Clean the surfaces outside your overhead ductwork.','overhead','This service addresses settled dust on the outside of exposed HVAC ducts and related accessible surfaces. It does not include internal duct cleaning, HVAC servicing or changes to ventilation equipment.', ['Exposed duct tops and accessible exterior faces','External HVAC housings where suitable','Coordination around suspended services and ceiling fixtures']),
('hepa-high-dusting','HEPA high dusting','Capture dust with a method suited to the material.','hero','Where suitable, HEPA-filtered vacuum equipment can support controlled dry dust extraction. Equipment selection depends on the dust characteristics and the site assessment; HEPA filtration alone does not make a system suitable for hazardous or combustible dust.', ['Source capture using suitable vacuum equipment','Dry extraction for compatible surfaces and dust','Separate assessment for hazardous or combustible materials']),
